 > Counts and observations describe their recorded checkpoints. Current rules and headline status live in [AGENTS.md](../../../AGENTS.md) and [STATUS.md](../../STATUS.md). The preceding [eleventh record](wave-48-part11.md) retains its original stage claims.
+
+W48-CMT-SELF-INIT-DISJOINT-FRAMES adds a bounded same-owner child-slot frame to rule 36b: source-bound Clang layout proves separation from initializer writes, the complete ledger/field/partial obligations survive, compatible alias facts are preserved, and other member facts are invalidated conservatively. Historical retyping, hidden rebinding, unsupported frames and overlap refuse; different allocation IDs provide no physical separation premise. Rust, 23 new Lean theorem checks and the canonical CFL initializer model (18 to 28 clauses, deliberately pinned) match; no interpreted initializer call permission is added. Fresh BASE 47fc52a32 -> prediction acb13489c/b593500d9 -> semantic TIP 342ca74c4 preserves corpus 1,013 Safe / 3,812 Unknown / 9 provisional Unsafe, system 101 / 343 / 4, and slice 57 Safe / 342 Unknown / 4 Pending / 1 provisional Unsafe, with zero Safe gain/loss, getter closure gain 0 and complete resource/NULL/runtime attribution. Full gate: 8,686 Rust (554 units/567 summaries, 0 failed/15 ignored), 373 Lean audits, 460 root Python, provider 133 Rust (1 ignored)/25 Python, all five packages and every gate command exit 0. The broader frame follow-up and CMetrics getter chain remain Open for foreign-owner, containment/member/collection relations, deeper/same-member paths, loaded/retyped pointer source forms, nonordinary calls, B08 source aliases and the remaining API adoption/hash/cache/borrow/label obligations. [Report](../../reports/cmt-self-init-disjoint-frames/README.md).
 
